      {
        "file": "platform/webcheck/history-blob.mjs",
        "issue": "readHistoryBlob treated every git failure in a shallow clone as 'history absent, skip': a wrong path at a commit the clone does carry (readHistoryBlob('.', 'HEAD', 'ventures/no-such-venture/index.html') in this session's shallow clone) returned ok:false with a reason claiming 'The blob exists in the repository's history', so a page-integrity test pinned to a renamed or mistyped path would skip in every web session instead of failing. Fixed: the skip now also requires the commit to be absent (git cat-file -e rev^{commit}); failing-first test 'a path missing at a revision the SHALLOW clone does carry still throws'.",
        "patched": true,
        "patched_in": "https://github.com/Duncan-Haywood/oss-monorepo/pull/18329"
      }
